      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed Arlington after General Robert E. Lee when the post office changed names in 1875.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/arlington-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Johnson Station, founded in 1846 by Middleton Tate Johnson, served as a frontier outpost and stagecoach stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/arlington-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Arlington College opened in 1895 as a private school, later becoming Carlisle Military Academy until 1913.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/arlington-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Ballpark in Arlington, built in 1994, hosted Super Bowl XLV in 2011 and the first College Football Championship Game in 2015.",
